{"hypotheses":"odd target DVR; t=v(Z)>0; a,A,D units; (A|kappa)=-1; k=v(b)>=0","label":"PROVED","name":"bridge-valuation-trichotomy","proof":"for k>0, Ng=16a^4b^2-A(b-1)^4 is congruent to -A; for k=0 its valuation is nonnegative","result":{"0<k<t":"v(c)=2(t-k)>0, hence Bbar=cbar=0","k=0":"v(c)>=2t, hence Bbar!=0 and cbar=0","k=t":"cbar=-a_bar^2*zeta^2/beta^2 and cbar^2 is a nonzero fourth power","k>t":"v(c)=2(t-k)<0"},"type":"theorem"}
{"Hensel":"rank two in a chosen pair of variables over the residue field is sufficient; total-space rank may use s or b when the fibre ramifies","label":"PROVED","name":"exact-eliminants-and-fibre-Jacobians","orientation_I":{"Q":"A*u^2+(A^2-c^2-16*A*B)*u+16*A^2*B*s^2-16*A","det_d(C1,C2)/d(y,r)":"4*y*r*(A*(y^2+r^2)-c^2-16*A*B)=4*y*r*Q_I'(u)","squares":["u","A+u=y^2"],"u":"r^2"},"orientation_II":{"Q":"A*u^2-(c^2+16*A*B)*u+16*A^2*B*(s^2-1)-16*A","det_d(C1',C2')/d(y,r)":"4*y*r*(c^2+16*A*B-2*A*u)=-4*y*r*Q_II'(u)","squares":["u","A+u=r^2"],"u":"y^2"},"type":"theorem"}
{"character_sum":"K_q=[q+S_C-S_A-T+n_C(1-epsilon)-2n_A]/4 for A+4 square or zero; M_q=[q+S_C-S_A-T+n_C(epsilon-1)-2n_A]/4 for A+4 nonzero square","conclusion":"the plus arm exists for every odd q except F_9; F_9 has a fibre-regular minus-arm point. For prime w>=5 a nonzero-square A+4 may be chosen, giving fibrewise Hensel; w=3 is lifted on the s-chart.","curve":"T=sum_a chi((1+4a^2)(5+4a^2)); if char!=5, #E(F_q)=q+T+2 for E:v^2=(1+4x^2)(5+4x^2), so |T+1|<=2sqrt(q)","exact_counts":{"I":"(q-1)*sum_{chi(A)=-1,u}(1+chi(u))(1+chi(A+u))*1_{u(A+u)=16}","II":"2*(q-1)*sum_{chi(A)=-1}[(1+chi(A+4))+1_{chi(-1)=1}(1+chi(A-4))]","normalization":"q-1 choices of beta=b/pi^k are included"},"finite_cases":[3,5,7,9],"hypotheses":"odd residue field F_q; 0<k<t; A=1+4a^2 is a nonsquare","label":"PROVED","name":"low-positive-uniform-local-solubility","orientation_II_plus_arm":"u=4, y=+-2, r^2=A+4","reduction":{"I":"u*(A+u)=16","II":"u^2=16, i.e. u=+4 or u=-4"},"target_consequence":"t=3*v_w(z)>=3, so k=1 always lies in this theorem","type":"theorem"}
{"Hensel":"when n*d!=0, dC2/db=32*A*d is a unit and one nonzero y/r derivative of C1 supplies rank two","exact_count":"N_O=sum_{chi(A)=-1,u}(1+chi(u))(1+chi(A+u))*L_q(n_O,d_O), where L=q-1 if n=d=0, L=1 if n*d!=0, and L=0 otherwise","existence":"for q>=17, the orientation-II hyperbola has q-1 ordered points and at most 12 lie over n*d=0; q=3,5,7,9,11,13 are exhausted exactly","hypotheses":"k=0, so B=2b is nonzero and cbar=0","label":"PROVED","name":"unit-residue-system-and-count","orientation_I":"n_I=u^2+A*u-16, d_I=A*s^2-u, n_I+16*B*d_I=0","orientation_II":"n_II=u^2-16, d_II=A*(s^2-1)-u, n_II+16*B*d_II=0","type":"theorem"}
{"bridge":"cbar=-g^2 with g=a*zeta/beta, hence cbar^2=g^4 and g ranges F_q^* with beta","counts":{"I":"sum (1+chi(u))(1+chi(A+u))*nu_4(A*(u^2+A*u-16)/u)","II":"sum (1+chi(u))(1+chi(A+u))*nu_4(A*(u^2-16)/u)","nu_4":"#{g in F_q^*:g^4=x}"},"hypotheses":"k=t; write Z=pi^t*zeta and b=pi^t*beta","integrality":"unit leading and constant coefficients force every local root u to be a unit, so residue square tests are necessary","label":"PROVED","name":"critical-residue-system","obstruction":"q=5 has count zero in both orientations on the entire k=t, nonsquare-A residue stratum","type":"theorem"}
{"conclusion":"neither orientation has a local point","hypotheses":"k>t and A is a nonsquare unit","label":"PROVED","name":"pole-range-obstruction","newton":"each eliminant has root valuations +4(k-t) and -4(k-t)","proof":"a positive-valuation square u makes A+u reduce to nonsquare A; a negative-valuation root satisfies u/(c^2/A)=1 mod pi, so u has nonsquare class A^{-1}","type":"theorem"}
{"bridge_bound":"on Phi, v2(c)>=4: v2(Ng)>=4 and v2(D)=0 for v2(Z)>=0, while v2(D)=2v2(Z) for v2(Z)<0","consequence":"both diagonal orientations are Phi-empty over Q_2; the odd target-place theorem cannot produce a global five-unknown definition","exact_modular_checks":{"orientation_I":256,"orientation_II":8192},"label":"PROVED","orientation_I":"Q_I/A has coefficient valuations (4,0,0); roots have v2(u)=4 or 0, and A+u is respectively 5 or 6 mod 8, never a square","orientation_II":"Q_II/A=u^2-32h*u+16e with h,e odd; roots have v2(u)=2. Writing u=4t^2 gives mod 16 the impossible congruence 8+2Ab(s^2-1)=0","parity_split":"v2(s^2-1)=0 for s even and >=3 for s odd, so the last congruence has valuation 1 or residue 8 mod 16","source":["math/h10q/l24_diagonal_geometry.py","math/h10q/data/l24_diagonal_geometry.jsonl","/tmp/l24_diagonal_geometry.md"],"type":"dyadic-global-supersession"}
